---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [["Can I use the same reporting address for TLS-RPT and DMARC rua=?", "Yes, the same mailbox can receive both TLS-RPT and DMARC reports. They are different formats and can be distinguished by content."], ["Does TLS-RPT require DNSSEC?", "No. TLS-RPT is a plain DNS TXT record and does not require DNSSEC validation."]];

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: "TLS-RPT Record",
  description: "TLS-RPT record: how to create the _smtp._tls DNS TXT record for SMTP TLS reporting. RFC 8460 syntax.",
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://promptdns.com/favicon.svg' } },
  datePublished: '2026-10-27',
  dateModified: '2026-10-27',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};

const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Email Authentication', item: 'https://promptdns.com/email-authentication/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "TLS-RPT Record" },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="TLS-RPT Record: How to Create the _smtp._tls DNS TXT Record for TLS Reporting"
  description="TLS-RPT record: how to create the _smtp._tls DNS TXT record for SMTP TLS reporting. RFC 8460 syntax."
  schema={[article, faqSchema, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">TLS-RPT Record</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">TLS-RPT Record</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-dim">TLS-RPT record: how to create the _smtp._tls DNS TXT record for SMTP TLS reporting.</p>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class='pdns-table' style='width:100%'><thead><tr><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Step</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='pd-mono'>1</td><td>Go to your DNS provider (Cloudflare, Namecheap, GoDaddy)</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>2</td><td>Add a TXT record with name: _smtp._tls.yourdomain.com</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>3</td><td>Set the value: v=TLSRPTv1; rua=mailto:tls-reports@yourdomain.com</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>4</td><td>Save and verify with our free tools</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Technical details</h2>
      <p class='mt-3'>A TLS-RPT record is a DNS TXT record published at _smtp._tls.domain.com that contains a v=TLSRPTv1 declaration and a rua= reporting address where mailbox providers deliver daily JSON reports about TLS connection outcomes.</p><p class='mt-3'>The record follows the syntax defined in RFC 8460 and must be published as a single TXT record at the exact name _smtp._tls.domain.com (not at the root or at a subdomain other than _smtp._tls).</p><p class='mt-3'>TLS-RPT is most useful when combined with MTA-STS: TLS-RPT provides the visibility into TLS failures while MTA-STS provides the enforcement mechanism.</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">TLS-RPT requires zero maintenance after deployment: the DNS record never changes, and the reports arrive automatically. It is the lowest-effort, highest-visibility DNS security improvement.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I use the same reporting address for TLS-RPT and DMARC rua=?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, the same mailbox can receive both TLS-RPT and DMARC reports. They are different formats and can be distinguished by content.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does TLS-RPT require DNSSEC?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No. TLS-RPT is a plain DNS TXT record and does not require DNSSEC validation.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Check your domain with our free tools:
        <a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SPF checker</a>,
        <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DMARC checker</a>,
        <a href="/dkim-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DKIM checker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
